==English==

===Etymology===
{{back-form|en|fluorescence}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/fləˈɹɛs/|/flʊəˈɹɛs/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛs|s=2}}
* {{hmp|en|floresce}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|physics}} To emit [[electromagnetic radiation]], especially [[visible]] light, when [[absorb]]ing radiation of some other [[wavelength]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1974|author=w:John Boorman|title=Zardoz|publisher=Pan Books|location=London|page=98|passage=The blinding light did not hurt, it filled him, he glowed, all his veins '''fluoresced''', each one alive with new growth.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|physics}} To cause to fluoresce; to make [[fluorescent]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2012|author=Oliver J. Wagner; Brian E. Louie; Eric Vallières; Ralph W. Aye; Alexander S. Farivar|title=Near-Infrared Fluorescence Imaging Can Help Identify the Contralateral Phrenic Nerve During Robotic Thymectomy|journal=w:The Annals of Thoracic Surgery|volume=94|doi=10.1016/j.athoracsur.2012.04.119|page=622|passage=During right robotic thymectomy, fluorescence imaging facilitates identification of the contralateral phrenic nerve by '''fluorescing''' the pericardiophrenic vessels.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} Of colours, to be very [[bright]]; to be so bright as to appear to radiate as a light source.

